Are there any designers/programmers that have good, applicable ideas (or actual
 PROGRAMS!) for games designed for multiple players (MORE than two) using ONE 
computer (NOT LAN games)?

The ACCESS.bus, an open industry peripheral connectivity standard, enables 
multiple users to each have his/her own I/O device all addressing the same 
ONE application simultaneously.
 
This new capability enables new applications, specifically: multiplayer games 
that run on ONE computer (like a four-player flight sim with real-time 
dogfights...?), instead of over a network.

Of course there are some design and interface challenges, such as 
the monitor problem (How do two players compete in a "Battleships" game when 
_both_ are looking at the same screen???), etc. Some current games easily lend 
themselves to multi-joystick or multi-keyboard (multi-player) versions, and 
others require a great deal of rethinking and re-design. The potential is big 
and the implementation of games that take full advantage of ACCESS.bus' "plug 
and Play" and multi-device-one-computer capabilities is intriguing...

Any thoughts, remarks and good ideas?

